Foreign formal-language content a DSL owns — mathematics and code, embedded when small and exhibited when large.

<section #ag-align | `<align>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<align>`.

<code-block #code:ag-align-1>
<align>
x^2 + y^2 &= z^2 \\
a + b &= c
</align>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-align-1>
<align>
x^2 + y^2 &= z^2 \\
a + b &= c
</align>
</minipage>

*Two aligned equations. The `&amp;` marks the alignment column (here,
the `=` sign). Handler wraps in `\begin{aligned}...\end{aligned}`
(KaTeX-compatible variant of LaTeX's `align`).*

</section>

<section #ag-cases | `<cases>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<cases>`.

<code-block #code:ag-cases-1>
<cases>
x^2 & \text{if } x \ge 0 \\
-x^2 & \text{if } x < 0
</cases>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-cases-1>
<cases>
x^2 & \text{if } x \ge 0 \\
-x^2 & \text{if } x < 0
</cases>
</minipage>

*A two-case piecewise definition. Handler wraps in
`\begin{cases}...\end{cases}`.*

</section>

<section #ag-code | `<code>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<code>`.

<code #code:ag-code-1>
The function is `factorial`.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-code-1>
The function is `factorial`.
</minipage>

*Plain markdown backticks produce inline &lt;code&gt;. The most common
authoring path.*

</section>

<section #ag-code-block | `<code-block>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<code-block>`.

<code #code:ag-code-block-1>
<``` python | print("hello, world") ```>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-code-block-1>
<``` python | print("hello, world") ```>
</minipage>

*The triple-backtick sigil. The first positional token is the
language (emitted as a `language-X` class on the &lt;code&gt;); the pipe
separates it from the verbatim, whitespace-preserving content — the
pipe-form padding (the spaces around the content) is KEPT, since
whitespace in code is significant and visible to the reader. (#327)*

</section>

<section #ag-display-math | `<display-math>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<display-math>`.

<code #code:ag-display-math-1>
<$$ \sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i = X $$>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-display-math-1>
<$$ \sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i = X $$>
</minipage>

*The `$$` sigil. Display-mode LaTeX rendered by KaTeX on its own line;
numbered by default (the equation number is appended after the KaTeX
output).*

</section>

<section #ag-eqnarray | `<eqnarray>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<eqnarray>`.

<code-block #code:ag-eqnarray-1>
<eqnarray>
f(x) &=& x^2 \\
g(x) &=& 2x
</eqnarray>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-eqnarray-1>
<eqnarray>
f(x) &=& x^2 \\
g(x) &=& 2x
</eqnarray>
</minipage>

*Two equations rendered via KaTeX's `aligned` env (the supported
equivalent of LaTeX's `eqnarray`).*

</section>

<section #ag-inline-code | `<inline-code>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<inline-code>`.

<code #code:ag-inline-code-1>
Assign with <` x = 1 `> at the top of the function.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-inline-code-1>
Assign with <` x = 1 `> at the top of the function.
</minipage>

*The single-backtick sigil. With no pipe, the whole body is opaque
code content rendered as &lt;code&gt; (the same output as a markdown
backtick span). Whitespace in code is significant and preserved, so
the pipe-form padding stays INSIDE the &lt;code&gt;. (#327)*

</section>

<section #ag-inline-math | `<inline-math>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<inline-math>`.

<code #code:ag-inline-math-1>
The identity <$ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 $> holds for right triangles.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-inline-math-1>
The identity <$ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 $> holds for right triangles.
</minipage>

*The `$` sigil. Opaque LaTeX content rendered inline by KaTeX and
wrapped in &lt;inline-math&gt; for CSS targeting. The sigil carries no
attributes — id and classes are not supported for inline math.*

</section>

<section #ag-math | `<math>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<math>`.

<code-block #code:ag-math-1>
<math>
E = mc^2
</math>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-math-1>
<math>
E = mc^2
</math>
</minipage>

*Long-form `&lt;math&gt;` block. Semantically equivalent to the
`&lt;$$ E = mc^2 $$&gt;` display-math sigil — both render block-level
LaTeX math via KaTeX. Use the long-form when the source is
multi-line or when explicit tag bounds aid readability; use the
sigil for brevity.*

</section>

<section #ag-matrix | `<matrix>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<matrix>`.

<code-block #code:ag-matrix-1>
<matrix>
1 & 2 \\
3 & 4
</matrix>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-matrix-1>
<matrix>
1 & 2 \\
3 & 4
</matrix>
</minipage>

*A 2×2 matrix. The handler wraps the body in
`\begin{matrix}...\end{matrix}` before KaTeX renders.*

</section>

<section #ag-footnote-sigil | The `<^ …>` footnote sigil>

Notation's sigils have one sibling outside this family: the footnote sigil. It is
listed here because this chapter is where the sigil forms live side by side.

<code #code:ag-caret-1>
A claim<^ A footnote written with the sigil.>.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-caret-1>
A claim<^ A footnote written with the sigil.>.
</minipage>

*The `^` sigil (#416): the native footnote, sugar for `<note | …>` —
`<^ x>` and `<note | x>` produce byte-identical output. Content-only (no
id or attributes inside the sigil); see `<note>` in the Aside chapter for
the attributed and long forms, numbering, and margin placement.*

</section>
